Month = {AUG},
Abstract = {The 5.5MV CN-Van de Graaff (VDG) accelerator was first installed and
   operated in the early 50's at Rice University (Houston, TX) and it was
   donated to IFUNAM ({''}Instituto de Fisica, Universidad Nacional
   Autonoma de Mexico{''}) in 1984 and started a new life in 1988. At the
   end of 2017, the ion source was severely damaged. Several power supplies
   were destroyed. In this article we describe the process of restoring the
   VDG terminal. A number of power supplies were redesigned, built, tested
   and mounted in the Terminal. As a result of the work carried out during
   most of 2019, the VDG accelerator is now operational and we show data
   from the Rutherford Backscattering (RBS) analysis of a platinum coated
   silicon slab using the first proton and.. beams. Electronic diagrams of
   all supplies in their new configuration are provided for the benefit of
   this kind of RF-Ion sources users still numerous.},
