Abstract = {Palaeodiplothrombidium microscutum gen. et sp. nov. is described based
   on one adult and one deutonymph preserved in early Miocene amber from
   Chiapas Mexico. This new taxon is the first record for the Parasitengona
   Cohort (Acari: Trombidiformes: Prostigmata) for the Chiapas amber and is
   also the first fossil record for the Johnstonianidae Family, worldwide.},
